  Cell["4. Quantum energy, corrected radius and spin reduction", "Section"], 
  Cell["Equation (18) is evaluated with exactly matched radial and angular \
cutoffs in the eigenvalue sum and Tr F. For m>0 one block contains both \
angular sectors; its contribution is (sum Abs[eigenvalues]-Tr Fm-Tr \
FminusM)/2. For m=0 it is (sum positive energies-Tr F0)/2. A stable vacuum is \
required. In a 2D continuum the joint high-momentum zero-point sum is cutoff \
dependent; N=40 justifies low modes, not an unregulated energy trace. The \
quantum curves below are explicitly finite-cutoff results, with separate \
radial and angular sensitivity tables.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[
     {RowBox[{RowBox[{"quantum", "[", RowBox[{"p_Association", ",", 
            "n_Integer", ",", "q_Integer", ",", "mm_Integer"}], "]"}], ":=", 
        RowBox[{"quantum", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"p", "[", "\"b\"", "]"}], 
            ",", RowBox[{"p", "[", "\"R\"", "]"}], ",", "n", ",", "q", ",", 
            "mm"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"quantum", "[", RowBox[
           {RowBox[{"bb_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", RowBox[{"radius_", "?", 
              "NumericQ"}], ",", "n_Integer", ",", "q_Integer", ",", 
            "mm_Integer"}], "]"}], ":=", 
        RowBox[{RowBox[{"quantum", "[", RowBox[{"bb", ",", "radius", ",", 
              "n", ",", "q", ",", "mm"}], "]"}], "=", 
          RowBox[{"Module", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[
                 {RowBox[{"p", "=", RowBox[{"profile", "[", RowBox[{"bb", 
                        ",", "radius"}], "]"}]}], ",", "blocks", ",", "emin", 
                  ",", "eq", ",", "parts", ",", "s", ",", "st"}], "}"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{RowBox[{"blocks", "=", RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
                    RowBox[{RowBox[{"sector", "[", RowBox[{"p", ",", "m", 
