      "Output"]}, Open]], Cell["Coverage: topology and classical texture \
(Eqs. 2-9, Figs. 1-4); local frame and continuum identities (Appendix A); \
Bessel/BdG spectrum and disk instability (Eqs. 10-17, Appendix B, Figs. 5-6); \
matched-cutoff quantum energy and radius shift (Eq. 18, Figs. 7-8); conical \
reference (Eq. 19, Appendix C, Fig. 9); normalized local spin reduction (Eqs. \
16,20, Fig. 10); edge matching and triangular lattice bands (Eq. 21, Fig. \
11); and the paper 3D approximation, radial BdG comparison and thermal \
infrared integrals (Eqs. 22-23). All plotted data are recomputed. The new \
notebook replaces the historical exploratory variants, including anisotropy, \
Neumann boundaries and multispiral trial states, with the model used in the \
paper.", "Text"], Cell["Limits: numerical plots use finite sampling and \
declared cutoffs. Quantum energy and its shifted optimum are \
regulator-dependent illustrations; no microscopic lattice cutoff or quantum \
spiral energy is supplied. Boundary tunneling remains approximate and has a \
documented amplitude ambiguity; negative estimates are diagnostic. The rigid \
3D shift and thermal unit-weight infrared estimates are explicitly separated \
from exact BdG operations. Figure 8's prose and plotted minimum disagree; the \
notebook reports its own finite-cutoff minimum rather than imposing either \
value.", "Text"], Cell["Independent numerical crosscheck: a separate SciPy \
solve_bvp profile solver and scipy.linalg.eig Bessel calculation at b=0.6, \
R=4, N=40, q=512 found epsilon(-1,0)=0.122187806779896 and \
epsilon(-2,0)=0.403446181028857; the literal Sec. III splittings were \
0.280033956292601 and 0.278079511899320. These agree with the Wolfram \
calculation using q=320. Increasing the independent calculation to N=80, \
q=1024 changes energies by less than 5e-13 and splittings by less than \
2.6e-6. These external checks are benchmarks, not dependencies or imported \
calculation data. The direct continuum-Hessian algebra was independently \
checked with SymPy.", "Text"]}, WindowSize -> {1440, 950}, 
